  "notes": "GAAP audit. Re-extracted from the re-trimmed PDF (13 pages; p2 Statement of Activities newly added, so all later pages moved by one: p3 governmental funds balance sheet, p4 governmental funds revenues/expenditures, p5-7 proprietary statements, p8-9 General Fund budget schedule, p10 Street, p11 Debt Service, p12 nonmajor combining, p13 General Fund combining). governmental_net_position from the Statement of Activities p2 (2,116,385 + 142,426 = 2,258,811). Governmental lines from p4 (Total Governmental Funds); its Taxes 689,440 is split using the p2 general revenue rows 'Taxes - Levied for general purposes' 657,966 (tax type not printed, stays taxes) and 'Taxes - Levied for bond services' 31,474 (the Municipal Building debt service fund's taxes, printed 'Property taxes' on its budget schedule p11). Fund balances 1,452,916 + 1,142,698 - 1,013,283 + 5,500 = 1,587,831 (p4). ending_cash as in FY2024 = governmental funds balance sheet cash and cash equivalents 1,114,840 + cash held by county treasurer 13,997 (p3); ending_investments = Certificate of Deposit 328,683 (p3). Business-type from the proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Fund Net Position (p6, Totals); no single printed total, so receipts/disbursements are operating + nonoperating sums; interest expense 105,628 (also printed on p2). Roll-forward 6,849,866 + 6,830,837 - 7,168,088 = 6,512,615. Proprietary cash flows from p7 Total column. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1). Detail: General Fund from the combining statement by department (p13; the General Fund budget schedule p8 is less detailed and not recorded); Street Fund budget schedule (p10); Municipal Building debt service fund (p11; Prairie Hills St. District has no activity); nonmajor funds per fund column (p12). The General Fund Transfer In 5,500 has no matching transfer out anywhere (decision_needed). Read pages 1-13 of 13"
}
